@page
@model KopiCinta.Pages.TeamRizaModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Riza Agung Pribadi";
}

<section class="section">
    <div class="container">

        <div class="back-top reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team">← Back</a>
        </div>

        <div class="event-hero reveal">
            <div class="event-hero-text">
                <p class="eyebrow">Our Team</p>
                <h2>Riza Agung Pribadi</h2>

                <p class="event-intro">
                    A finance team member who believes inclusion is not about helping,
                    but about creating real access so everyone can connect.
                </p>

                <div class="event-tags">
                    <span>Finance</span>
                    <span>Access</span>
                    <span>Inclusion</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="team-profile-hero-img reveal">
                <img src="/images/team/riza.jpg" alt="Riza Agung Pribadi">
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-block reveal">
            <div class="hbii-block-text">
                <p class="hbii-label">His Perspective</p>
                <h3>Creating Access That Is Often Overlooked</h3>

                <p>
                    Through his journey at Kopi Cinta, Riza learned that working with Deaf friends
                    is not just about collaboration, but about creating access that is often overlooked.
                </p>

                <p>
                    One of his most memorable experiences was accompanying Deaf friends
                    to learn about coffee directly at Wonosantri Coffee Plantation.
                </p>

                <p>
                    There, he saw how a simple opportunity can become truly meaningful
                    when access is provided.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-block-card">
                <h4>His Role</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li>Finance</li>
                    <li>Behind-the-scenes support</li>
                    <li>Program sustainability</li>
                    <li>Operational support</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-feature reveal">
            <div class="hbii-feature-card">
                <p class="hbii-label">Meaning</p>
                <h3>Quiet Work, Real Impact</h3>

                <p>
                    In the team, Riza takes on a role in finance—
                    a role that may not always be visible,
                    but plays an important part in keeping everything running.
                </p>

                <p>
                    From this, he realized that impact doesn’t always have to be seen.
                    Sometimes, it grows quietly—
                    yet still carries meaning.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="hbii-feature-card soft">
                <p class="hbii-label">Purpose</p>
                <h3>Starting with a Small Step</h3>

                <p>
                    Riza joined Kopi Cinta because of its strong social value,
                    especially in spreading Deaf awareness to more people.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Through his experience, he hopes to encourage others
                    not to be afraid to start communicating with Deaf friends.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Because from that small step,
                    we begin to understand and open access to information
                    that has long been limited.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="hbii-ending reveal">
            <h3>His Reflection</h3>

            <p>
                For Riza, inclusion is not about helping—
                it is about ensuring everyone can connect.
            </p>
        </div>

        <br />

        <div class="detail-back reveal">
            <a asp-page="/Team" class="btn btn-secondary">← Back to Team</a>
        </div>

    </div>
</section>